* A flux-tunable transmon coupled to a readout resonator.
*
* The single junction of a transmon is replaced by a SQUID, so flux 1 tunes the
* qubit through the resonator. Nothing in this file says "coupling strength": the
* vacuum Rabi splitting follows from the 6 fF capacitor.

.title  Tunable transmon with readout resonator
.name   tunable_transmon_readout

J1  1  0  Ic=40nA  Cj=2fF       ; SQUID, junction A
J2  1  0  Ic=28nA  Cj=2fF       ; SQUID, junction B (asymmetric)
C1  1  0  70fF                  ; transmon shunt
Cc  1  2  6fF                   ; coupling capacitor
L2  2  0  2nH                   ; resonator
C2  2  0  250fF

.flux   1 = 0.0
.options ext_basis=harmonic
.cutoff n1   = 14
.cutoff ext2 = 16               ; check_convergence reports 2 MHz of error at 8
.levels 6
.end
